															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zmax15" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2000203); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2000203&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606142819" alt="Zmax15" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2000203)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zmax15" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2000203); return false;" >Zmax15</a></span> <span class="odate time_1436601036 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">11 Jul 2015 07:50</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2335977">
									

<p>Phenomenal concept work. It's amazing what can be done with a jokey premise, or even just making anything out of these weird concepts we as a species have created for ourselves, like tentacle porn. I also like that the 'Lovecraftian horror' is the follower of humanity. The whole thing melds so well into cohesive picture of what this is and why, without telling everything is something to look up to in writing. The few negatives (see below) barely touch the good. You have a hearty +1 from me!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">the&nbsp;smallest&nbsp;of&nbsp;complaints</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">the&nbsp;smallest&nbsp;of&nbsp;boxes</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>If I had to comment on what could be improved, I'd say three things. First, sentient in the first footnote probably would not be the best term for cephalopods, given it usually brings thoughts to intelligent rather than animate. Second, the description says that SCP-2698-A is capable of accessing the internet, which should probably be altered to saying it can access networks connected to SCP-2698, including the internet. The third, that the forewords of the -A interviews should probably be two sentences like the other one, or separated with a semicolon or something.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

