<blockquote>
<p>the 'Lovecraftian horror' is the follower of humanity.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Not really, humans are deemed infants to 2698-A. It's just that it does not know that humans are speaking to it. As far as 2698-A is concerned, it is communing with the gods a la Moses on Mount Sinai. It would only feel scandalised if it knew the people behind the words.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>First, sentient in the first footnote probably would not be the best term for cephalopods, given it usually brings thoughts to intelligent rather than animate.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I wanted to include the possibility of robotic tentacles or even vines&#8230; although I can understand your intent behind &quot;animate&quot;.</p>

